From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:06:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Players go with their world onto its own thread

A world with players can now tick on its own thread. Its players' packets,
connection ticks (keep-alive, idle kick), commands, synchronous chat callbacks
and quits run there: a packet queued for the server thread before the move is
handed on when it runs, ServerConnection leaves those connections to the world
thread and posts their disconnects there, NetworkManager writes and drains for
the thread that owns the connection, and each thread batches its own sends.
Chunk loads and shapes finish on the thread of their world, and a world on its
own thread decorates there under the decoration lock. Player-side timers (item
drops, book edits, digging, AthenaGuard) count the player's world's tick, time
updates go out by the world's tick, and the player maps are concurrent.

Still not: changing worlds into or out of such a world (teleports are refused,
a respawn stays in the world, a login never lands in it), and the main world.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

